# Project specific
runs/
# Block top-level `assets/` content but allow descent into `assets/images/`
# (a `assets/` blanket rule prevents Git from descending at all, so a leaf
# negation can't re-include any file underneath — using `assets/*` keeps the
# directory traversable).
assets/*
!assets/images/
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.png
*.usda
*.usdz
*.usdc
*.usd
*.mdl
*.faiss
!docs/images/*
# Public-shipping media under `assets/images/` (README teasers, doc images,
# screenshots, MP4s, etc.). The negation has to come AFTER the per-extension
# blocks above (`*.gif`, `*.png`, …) so it wins last-match.
!assets/images/**
!apps/texture_agent/data/examples/*/sources/usd/*.usd
!apps/texture_agent/examples/**/*.png
!apps/material_agent/data/examples/**/*.usd
!apps/material_agent/data/examples/**/*.usda
!apps/material_agent/data/examples/**/*.usdc
!apps/material_agent/data/examples/**/*.usdz
